        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(active-memory): accept max thinking config",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users configuring active-memory with `thinking: \"max\"` could have the value rejected by plugin manifest/schema metadata even though the runtime and docs already treat `max` as a valid thinking level.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis updates the active-memory manifest config enum to match the runtime contract and adds a schema regression so the accepted config value stays aligned.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can configure active-memory's maximum thinking level without manifest-driven validation rejecting the documented value.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/active-memory/config.test.ts`\n- `git diff --check upstream/main..HEAD`\n",
